{"resourceIdentifier":"3226","resourceName":"Padang Tikar Landscape","description":"The Padang Tikar Landscape project is located in the Padang Tikar Landscape of the Batu Ampar subdistrict, Kubu Raya district, West Kalimantan province, Indonesia. The project consists of 10 'Village Forests', covering 76,370 hectares (ha), 58,672.7 ha of which is eligible for the reducing emissions from deforestation and forest degradation (REDD) project. The Village Forest of Padang Tikar is the largest 'Village Forest' permit in Indonesia and is divided\r\ninto three types of forest: protected forest (69,299 ha), limited production forest (1,985 ha), and convertible production forest (5,086 ha). The Padang Tikar Landscape project is a microcosm of the country as it has comprehensive forest ecosystems, ranging from inland forests to swamp forests (including mangrove forests and peatlands).","location":{"latitude":0.831275,"longitude":109.313833},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-09-19","endExclusive":"2022-10-20","endInclusive":"2022-10-19"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3226"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"West Kalimantan province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Withdrawn"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"590557"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"REDD; WRC"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0007"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"58673 Hectares"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 30/08/20